  "comment": "Static refusals the node makes BEFORE its approval gate, so the plugin hook can refuse without prompting. Source of truth is the node; app/node/tests/test_approval_preflight_contract.py asserts every value here equals the node's own tables and the TypeScript plugin tests read this file. Order on the node: unknown-parameter check, then path or slug policy, then the approval gate. Conservative rule: the plugin refuses a slug or path only when it is a plain ASCII string (no whitespace, control or non-ASCII characters), plus an absent slug and unknown parameter names; anything else is left to the node. Not covered: add-on allowlist (node env config) and value-shape validation (node only). ha.config.helpers update and delete additionally accept one `<helper_type>_id` key.",
